<title>FRANCE: French consumer prices fell 0.2-0.3 pct in Aug.</title>
<headline>French consumer prices fell 0.2-0.3 pct in Aug.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics institute INSEE gave the following provisional data:</p>
<p>				    Aug	  July     Aug 1995</p>
<p> Month-on-month inflation -0.2-0.3     -0.2	 0.4</p>
<p> Year-on-year inflation    1.6-1.7	2.3	 1.9</p>
<p> CPI Index (base 1990)   113.6-113.7   113.9    111.8</p>
<p>INSEE gave the following breakdown of the consumer price index for all households in mainland France, base 1990.</p>
<p>     Category		  Weight(pct) index  1-mo   3-mo  yr/yr</p>
<p> Food excluding tobacco	 20.17    106.2  -1.2   -1.8    0.9</p>
<p> Private-sector manufactures  33.05    108.3   0.2   -0.6    0.8</p>
<p> Private-sector services	19.76    125.3   0.1    0.6    2.9</p>
<p> Energy				8.25    110.8   0.0   -0.9    3.7</p>
<p> Public services ex energy     6.58    126.9  -0.7   -0.2    1.0</p>
<p> Rent, water			 6.55    129.1   0.2    0.5    2.5</p>
<p> Health spending		   5.64    110.0   0.0    0.3    1.1</p>
<p> Total excluding tobacco	98.06    112.7  -0.2   -0.5    1.5</p>
<p>Cumulative inflation in the first eight months of 1996 was between 1.0 and 1.1 percent.</p>
<p>Paris newsroom +33 1 42 21 53 81</p>
